      ":question/problem": "If $C$ is a $12\\times 10$ matrix that has $5$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{rank}(C)=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\text{rank}(C)$ is the number of pivot columns in $C.$ \n\nSince $C$ has $10$ columns and $5$ of them are non-pivots, then the number of pivot columns in $C$ is \n\n$$\n10-5=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(C)=5.$",
